Package: chaosrcpp
Type: Package
Title: Chaotic Dynamical Systems in Rcpp with Precision Control and Recurrence Quantification Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Andrii", "Patrikei", email = "andriipatrikei@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2015-4843"))
Description: Fast compiled integrators and iterators for classic chaotic
    systems. The Lorenz and Roessler flows are integrated with a
    fourth-order Runge-Kutta kernel templated on the floating-point type, so
    the same code runs in single precision, double precision and a
    double-double type of about 106 bits, with an arbitrary-precision 'Rmpfr'
    run as the gold-standard reference. This makes it possible to watch
    rounding error alone drive two identical initial conditions apart on a
    chaotic attractor. Also included are Lyapunov spectra by Gram-Schmidt
    reorthonormalisation, the logistic, Henon, Ikeda and Chirikov standard
    maps with bifurcation diagrams and Lyapunov exponents, recurrence plots
    and Recurrence Quantification Analysis measures (RR, DET, L, Lmax, ENTR,
    LAM, TT and more), plotting helpers including an interactive 3D view, a
    benchmark against 'deSolve' and a 'shiny' explorer.
